## Findings fixed, one line each:
# FIND-001 (critical): skills/economy/gig/lib/ensure-gas.mjs -- appendDripLog now runs immediately
#   after broadcast (sent.hash obtained), BEFORE waitForTransactionReceipt -- no exception path can
#   leave a broadcast drip uncounted against the daily cap.
# FIND-002 (critical): skills/economy/lending/lib/lending-orchestrator.mjs -- runLockedIssuance now
#   calls isBorrowerEligibleWithReputationGate (not the raw isBorrowerEligible) at step 6, wired via
#   deps.reputationGate/deps.reputationGateFn; default (unconfigured) behavior unchanged (fail-open).
# FIND-003 (major): skills/economy/gig/__tests__/ensure-gas.test.mjs -- 2 new tests cover both
#   exception branches (sendDripFn throws pre-broadcast; waitForTransactionReceipt throws
#   post-broadcast, proving the FIND-001 fix via a same-cap retry that must NOT re-broadcast).
# FIND-004 (major): skills/economy/lending/lib/__tests__/lending-gate-reputation-composition.test.mjs
#   -- removed all 3 `if (!base.eligible) return;` silent early-exits, replaced with a loud
#   `assert.equal(base.eligible, true, ...)`; this surfaced a genuine fixture bug (wrong field names)
#   which is now fixed by reusing lending-gate.test.mjs's own known-good BASE_BORROWER shape.
# FIND-005 (major): PROP-043/044/045 (live Base Sepolia E2E) re-confirmed honestly NOT-RUN this round
#   too -- see evidence/e2e-status.md's round-2 note and specs/verification-architecture.md's round-2
#   re-confirmation note. No E2E was fabricated or simulated to close this finding.

